        "example": "Discretization error significantly impacts the trustworthiness of closed loop controllers because it can cause divergence between the optimized trajectory and the actual dynamics of the system. As the number of time steps increases, this error can accumulate, leading to solutions that become unreliable, especially in complex environments like satellite orbit or space shuttle landing. To mitigate these issues, methods like linear model predictive control (LMPC) can be used, which are designed to handle these limitations effectively."
    },
